Replaced the native HTML5 tab drag from ad5a952 with @dnd-kit.

Why not the smaller fixes:
- draggable="false" on the child buttons looks like the obvious fix and does
  nothing. Per the HTML spec the source node is 'the first element, going up the
  ancestor chain, starting at the node that the user tried to drag, that has
  draggable set to true' - a false descendant does not stop the walk.
- A delay/threshold is impossible with native DnD. The spec says explicitly that
  thresholds 'remain platform-dependent'. That is the whole reason this bug is
  macOS-only: WebKit (Safari, and Tauri's WKWebView) starts a drag from a press
  on a text node, Chromium wants travel first. Owning the gesture via pointer
  events is the only way to get a threshold.

Things that cost time and will again:
- createSortable alone does NOT reorder. Without onDragOver updating state, the
  source's index stays at initialIndex forever and drag-end sees no change -
  even though operation.target is correctly populated. The move() helper from
  @dnd-kit/helpers in onDragOver is what keeps dnd-kit's indices in step,
  because it reads them back from the rendered order.
- Mid-drag the strip holds two extra elements: a position:fixed overlay with
  [data-dnd-dragging] and a [data-dnd-placeholder] marking the landing slot.
  Any selector matching tabs must exclude them or hit strict-mode violations.
  They also linger through the drop animation, so tests must wait them out.
- DragDropProvider injects role=status live regions. That broke an unrelated
  runner-image test whose getByRole('status') suddenly matched 3 elements.
- Playwright's dragTo cannot drive this: it moves too directly to clear the
  activation distance. Tests need mouse.down, a short move to arm, then a
  stepped move. See dragTab in workspace.spec.ts.
- Two providers, not one: both strips render the same tab ids simultaneously
  (the inactive one is CSS-hidden, still in the DOM) and ids must be unique
  within a provider.

Deliberate behaviour changes, flagged to the user:
- Dropping into trailing empty strip space no longer appends. Sortable inserts
  at the hovered tab's index; restoring append needs a droppable on the strip.
- dnd-kit sets role=button on the tab container, so the close button is now a
  button nested inside a role=button. Works, but it is an a11y smell.

NOT VERIFIED: the bug is WebKit-only and this container has Chromium on Linux
only. 163 e2e tests pass and a regression test covers label/close clicks, but
the actual macOS fix is unconfirmed. The user must check on their Mac.
